            <chunk name="Object" index="1">
              <items count="3">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">4f2b8c1e-93d7-4a60-b5e2-7c1d0a9e3f64</item>
                <item name="Lib" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">82b21a65-da8f-433c-93fb-f9814609e1d6</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">LiDAR Site</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="6">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Fetch open LiDAR and building footprints for a site from its latitude and longitude, for City Surface: the footprints over a square of the given Size, the point cloud (the terrain) over a larger square, Terrain Size — the ground a CFD domain stands on reaches further than the buildings that matter. The Netherlands: AHN (Het Waterschapshuis, CC-BY 4.0) from its official sheets — a sheet is ~5 GB and is downloaded once into the cache, then every site in it is read from there — with BAG footprints (Kadaster, CC0). The United States: USGS 3DEP (public domain), only the point-cloud nodes over the site, with GlobalBuildingAtlas footprints (TUM, CC BY-NC 4.0; OpenStreetMap if it cannot be read). France (IGN LiDAR HD, Licence Ouverte), Switzerland (swissSURFACE3D, swisstopo), Bavaria (CC BY 4.0), Scotland (National LiDAR Programme, OGL) and Estonia (Maa- ja Ruumiamet): the 1 km tiles over the site, 65-155 MB each, cached once, with the same footprints. Everything comes out in metres around the site centre: wire Point Cloud, Footprints and Domain into City Surface. Tree Crowns are read from the cloud's own vegetation returns (one closed mesh per cluster, for the Tree component); Trees, Barriers and Furniture are for looking at and for a render (round trees; with Roads on, OpenStreetMap fences, walls, hedges and street furniture); Layer Outlines, Layer Names, Layer Roughness and Flatten are OpenStreetMap land cover (ODbL) with its Davenport z0, in the footprints' frame — wire them into the City Surface inputs of the same names. Rivers, streams and canals mapped as lines come with them as water ribbons (the OpenStreetMap width tag, else river 20 m, canal 8 m, stream 3 m).

