                        <chunk name="InputParam" index="9">
                          <items count="9">
                            <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Who thins the ground raster and scores the roof planes. Auto: the OpenCL GPU when there is one, else the CPU. GPU: the OpenCL GPU; a fallback to the CPU is reported, never silent. CPU: every core. The surface is the same either way — the GPU reproduces the CPU's cell means, medians and plane choices; the sequential triangulation stays on the CPU.</item>
                            <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">fd13731f-194f-42d8-ba40-9449f2ac65ef</item>
