                    <chunk name="param_input" index="8">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Where the ground comes from. GEDTM30: global bare-earth model, 30 m (CC BY 4.0) - the default. Auto: the regional bare-earth model that covers the site (Canada HRDEM, else USGS 3DEP), else GEDTM30. USGS 3DEP: the 1 m lidar DEM where a project covers the site, else ~10 m, then ~30 m, USA (public domain). Canada HRDEM: lidar DTM at 1 m, then 2 m, where flown, Canada (Open Government Licence - Canada). Copernicus GLO-30: global but a SURFACE model - buildings and trees are in the heights, so building massing seated on it stands too high (use only where nothing else covers the site). Each is read straight from its public bucket, no key. A source with no data at the site gives flat ground and says so in the Report. Optional; default GEDTM30.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">7e45e1bd-10f2-4e91-94a4-25d5e980073e</item>
